## Rename Simulation to Intelligence and group graph analysis by analysis type
================================================================================

Context: The top-level menu is **Intelligence** (`menu_config.json` id
`intelligence`, route `/intelligence/`). Simulation is one feature under it,
next to Community, Cohorts and Patterns. The backend packages, frontend
assets, templates and page route now follow that taxonomy. `back/core/graph_analysis`
is split into topic sub-packages by type of analysis (community, cohort,
pattern, metrics). External contracts keep their names: `/api/v1/simulations`,
MCP tools, the internal `/simulation/*` JSON API used by the Simulation feature,
the agents and the graph-DB `GraphSimulation` capability. No compatibility
shims: the old page URL `/simulation/` now returns 404.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/simulation/ -> src/back/objects/intelligence/
   Folder rename (module names unchanged). Imports updated in src, tests and
   tests/eval judges.
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/ -> topic sub-packages
   `community/` (JobCommunities, CommunityMaterializer, CommunityVocabulary),
   `cohort/` (CohortBuilder, CohortVocabulary), `pattern/` (JobPatterns,
   PatternMaterializer, PatternVocabulary, pattern_diagram), `metrics/`
   (JobMetrics). Shared job plumbing (LakeflowRunner, preflight, models,
   profiles) stays at the root. Each sub-package `__init__.py` re-exports its
   public names; the root `__init__.py` re-exports from them.
3. src/front/config/menu_config.json
   Menu id `simulation` -> `intelligence`, route `/simulation/` -> `/intelligence/`;
   groups `intelligence-community`, `intelligence-cohorts`,
   `intelligence-patterns`, `intelligence-simulation`.
