================================================================================
Save pattern snapshots in Unity Catalog instead of the graph
================================================================================

Context:
Intelligence > Patterns > Save wrote named Pattern individuals and :inPattern
triples into the domain graph ("Save & materialize"). The user only wants the
pattern result saved, with no materialization in the graph. Saved patterns now
live in a Delta table next to the pattern job output (graph_pattern_saved_<slug>),
written through the Build SQL warehouse. The RDF graph is never written. Each
saved pattern is a snapshot, so it survives the next Detect, which overwrites
graph_patterns_<slug>. Endpoints, task types, and labels are renamed from
"materialize" to "save" to match.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/SavedPatternStore.py (new)
   SavedPatternStore: save (INSERT ... SELECT from the output table filtered by
   pattern_id), list_saved (GROUP BY saved_id), members (bounded LIMIT/OFFSET),
   delete (one saved_id). Table DDL is idempotent; saved_id is validated; string
   literals escape quotes and backslashes.
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/JobPatterns.py
   Shared _domain_slug; new saved_pattern_table(output_schema, domain, graph_name).
3. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/PatternMaterializer.py (deleted)
   Graph-based save/list/delete replaced by SavedPatternStore.
4. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/PatternVocabulary.py (deleted)
   inPattern / Pattern URI helpers no longer used.
5. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/__init__.py,
   src/back/core/graph_analysis/__init__.py
   Re-export SavedPatternStore and saved_pattern_table; drop removed names.
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinAnalytics.py
   _pattern_warehouse helper shared by build_job_patterns and the new
   build_saved_patterns; save_pattern / list_saved_patterns /
   saved_pattern_members / delete_saved_pattern no longer take a graph store.
7. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py
   run_pattern_materialize_task -> run_pattern_save_task (no store argument);
   task message reports members, not triples.
8. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   POST /dtwin/patterns/materialize -> POST /dtwin/patterns/save (task_type
   pattern_save); saved list / members / delete no longer read the graph store.
9. src/front/static/intelligence/js/intelligence-patterns.js
   Endpoint and task type renamed; _materialize/_awaitMaterialize -> _save/_awaitSave.
10. src/front/static/global/js/task-tracker.js
    pattern_materialize -> pattern_save mapping.
11. src/front/templates/partials/intelligence/_intel_patterns.html
    Button and confirm read "Save"; copy says the graph is not changed.
12. src/front/templates/partials/intelligence/_intel_patterns_saved.html
    Copy describes snapshots in Unity Catalog; empty-state refers to Save.
13. src/front/templates/partials/layout/help_modal.html
    Saved entry text updated.
14. tests/units/core/test_saved_pattern_store.py (new)
    Save/list/members/delete on a SQLite stand-in for the warehouse; snapshot
    survives re-Detect; no graph writes; escaping; id validation; table names.
15. tests/units/core/test_pattern_materializer.py, tests/units/core/test_pattern_vocabulary.py (deleted)
16. tests/units/api/test_dtwin_patterns.py
    Save route and task-type assertions.
17. tests/units/front/test_intelligence_page_contract.py
    Save endpoint, pattern_save task type, and tracker mapping.
18. docs/architecture.md, docs/user-guide.md
    Pattern save described as a Unity Catalog snapshot; file reference updated.
19. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-pattern-detection-design.md (local, gitignored)
    Storage, API, and wording sections aligned with the snapshot design.

